  "title": "PR Lens workflow: guaranteed failure reason",
  "summary": "The PR Lens GitHub Actions workflow previously assumed the analyze step always wrote a reason file before failing; when the model call died early, the failure-reporting step read a missing file and the whole job broke instead of posting a useful comment. This change seeds the reason file with a fallback message before the analyze step runs, and makes the reporting step tolerate an empty or absent file by falling back to a literal string. The result is that a failed model call always produces a readable PR comment rather than a secondary shell error.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
